  ('39000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000037', 'Chris Nelson', 'R', '38000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000027', 'Public Service/Utility Commissioner, Public Service/Utility Commission (South Dakota; real office title in the source: "South Dakota Public Utilities Commission"), took office January 8, 2011. Sourced from Ballotpedia, verified 2026-08-12 directly against this state''s own PSC page (Selection Method + Total Seats + Length of term fields read individually, not inferred from party tags -- see migration header).'),
  ('39000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000038', 'Jeremy Oden', 'R', '38000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000028', 'Public Service/Utility Commissioner, Public Service Commission — Place 1 (Alabama; real office title in the source: "Alabama Public Service Commission Place 1"), took office December 3, 2012. Alabama''s PSC is mid-transition (Code of Alabama Title 37-1-1): moving from a 3-member at-large commission to a 7-member by-district commission, phased in through 2033 -- only 3 seats (President + Place 1 + Place 2) currently exist and are filled; Places 3-7 are not yet created, not merely vacant, so not modeled as offices here. The term length itself is also transitioning, from 4 years to 6, for commissioners serving from June 1, 2026 onward -- this migration uses 6 (the new constitutional standard going forward), though the current President''s own term began before that date under the old rule. Sourced from Ballotpedia, verified 2026-08-12 directly against this state''s own PSC page (Selection Method + Total Seats + Length of term fields read individually, not inferred from party tags -- see migration header).'),
  ('39000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000039', 'Chris Beeker, III', 'R', '38000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000029', 'Public Service/Utility Commissioner, Public Service Commission — Place 2 (Alabama; real office title in the source: "Alabama Public Service Commission Place 2"), took office September 24, 2024. Alabama''s PSC is mid-transition (Code of Alabama Title 37-1-1): moving from a 3-member at-large commission to a 7-member by-district commission, phased in through 2033 -- only 3 seats (President + Place 1 + Place 2) currently exist and are filled; Places 3-7 are not yet created, not merely vacant, so not modeled as offices here. The term length itself is also transitioning, from 4 years to 6, for commissioners serving from June 1, 2026 onward -- this migration uses 6 (the new constitutional standard going forward), though the current President''s own term began before that date under the old rule. Sourced from Ballotpedia, verified 2026-08-12 directly against this state''s own PSC page (Selection Method + Total Seats + Length of term fields read individually, not inferred from party tags -- see migration header).'),
  ('39000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000040', 'Cynthia Almond', 'R', '38000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000030', 'Public Service/Utility Commissioner, Public Service Commission — President (Alabama; real office title in the source: "Alabama Public Service Commission President"), took office June 16, 2025. Alabama''s PSC is mid-transition (Code of Alabama Title 37-1-1): moving from a 3-member at-large commission to a 7-member by-district commission, phased in through 2033 -- only 3 seats (President + Place 1 + Place 2) currently exist and are filled; Places 3-7 are not yet created, not merely vacant, so not modeled as offices here. The term length itself is also transitioning, from 4 years to 6, for commissioners serving from June 1, 2026 onward -- this migration uses 6 (the new constitutional standard going forward), though the current President''s own term began before that date under the old rule. Sourced from Ballotpedia, verified 2026-08-12 directly against this state''s own PSC page (Selection Method + Total Seats + Length of term fields read individually, not inferred from party tags -- see migration header).');
